# Cross-platform line-ending policy: every text file is committed AND checked
# out as LF on ALL platforms. This file overrides each machine's local
# core.autocrlf, so macOS and Windows working trees stay byte-identical and
# switching machines never produces line-ending diffs. (WoW reads LF fine;
# bash scripts REQUIRE LF; stylua.toml line_endings = "Unix" matches.)
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the important types (belt and suspenders)
*.lua text eol=lf
*.toc text eol=lf
*.xml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never converted
*.tga binary
